Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::a_guid_survives_the_on_disk_layout`.

The defect: a typo in the swap table repeats an index (`7, 7` where the third group should read
`7, 6`). `from_disk` then reads on-disk byte 7 twice and never reads byte 6, so one byte of every
GUID read off a disk is lost. What this harness proves is that the table is a permutation, which is
what makes `from_disk` and `to_disk` inverses; that it is the RIGHT permutation is the EFI System
Partition vector test in `guid.rs`, not this harness.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(guid::to_disk(guid::from_disk(bytes)), bytes)`.

diff --git a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/guid.rs b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/guid.rs
